  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "A bag contains two red balls and one blue ball. A ball is drawn without replacement from the bag until the blue ball is obtained. What is the expected number of balls drawn from the bag?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "2 balls",
      "worked": "Let $X$ be the number of balls drawn. The possible stopping sequences are B, RB and RRB.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X=1)&=\\frac13\\\\P(X=2)&=\\frac23\\times\\frac12=\\frac13\\\\P(X=3)&=\\frac23\\times\\frac12\\times1=\\frac13\\\\E(X)&=1\\times\\frac13+2\\times\\frac13+3\\times\\frac13\\\\E(X)&=2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe expected number drawn is 2 balls.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
